{
  "$comment": "Archived Lovable asset pointers. AC-1.4 deletes every `src/assets/*.asset.json` file, because a pointer imported by source code bakes a `/__l5e/assets-v1/...` path into the bundle that only Lovable's own hosting serves \u2014 the production 404 this whole pass began with. But the pointers are also the ONLY record of each asset's Lovable `asset_id`, `url`, `r2_key` and declared `size`/`content_type`, which is what makes re-recovery possible if a binary is ever lost. Deleting them outright would close the original bug and quietly throw away the disaster-recovery path at the same time. So they are archived here verbatim, outside `src/` where no bundler can reach them and where AC-1.3's scan does not look. scripts/recover-assets.ts reads this file when the pointer files are gone.",
  "archived_at": "2026-08-18",
  "count": 46,
